    "details": {
      "alignment": "Neutral",
      "type": {
        "value": "humanoid",
        "subtype": "Toad"
      },
      "cr": 2,
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><em>Waluipedia cast sheet — The Captain of the Palace Guard (955 BF).</em> Built by <code>tools/build-character-sheets.py</code>, generated from the article's own words. no XP ledger entry; archetype default → CR 2 as a officer. Numbers are a GM-ready reading of the record, not a filed stat line; the article stays the authority. Archive date 1040 BF.</p><p><strong>The Captain Who Stood Between the Fire and the Stair</strong> — Peach's Castle — Captain of the Palace Guard</p><p>Status: Deceased — killed by Bowser's fire in the hall of Peach's Castle on a night in Efferd, 955 BF, a month or so before the assassination; his sash left the castle on John Lee's arms</p><p>The head of the palace guard in the last month of the reign, known to the archive from one account and one night. He questioned a ceremonial guard for jumping, was warned by the same guard that the dungeon cell was unlocked and full of hoods, and did not get to answer, because Bowser came through the wall and breathed fire down the hall and the captain was standing between the fire and the stair to the royal apartments. His scorched sash is the one piece of him on the record, wound around both of John Lee's forearms.</p><h3>Evidence</h3><ul><li><strong>Sabre</strong> — “The Captain Who Stood Between the Fire and the Stair”</li><li><strong>Sneak Attack</strong> — “Deceased — killed by Bowser's fire in the hall of Peach's Castle on a night in Efferd, 955 BF, a month or so before the assassination; his sash left the castle on John Lee's arms”</li><li><strong>Leadership</strong> — “The Captain Who Stood Between the Fire and the Stair”</li></ul><p>Article: <code>#/article/captain_of_the_palace_guard_955</code> (characters). Site sheet: <code>#/sheets/captain_of_the_palace_guard_955</code>.</p>",
        "public": ""
      }
    },
